- `branch(b1, XOR)`: Missing guards on the outgoing edges to `n3` and `n4` to evaluate the conditions "If the article is available" and "if the article is not available".
- `defines(v1, ...)` and `defines(v2, ...)`: The variables are defined with empty ranges `{}` instead of valid value spaces.
- `action(n9, "has the customer accepted the offer")`, `branch(b2, XOR)`, `action(n11, "abort the enquiry and end process")`, and `end(e2)`: The model hallucinates an explicit evaluation and a rejection/abort path. The source text only specifies the positive progression ("Once the customer accepts the offer, we dispatch the article") and does not mention a rejection path.
- `actor(a_default, "Default", ...)`: The model assigns all nodes to a single "Default" actor, failing to distinguish between the responsibilities of the "customer" (e.g., making the enquiry) and "we" (e.g., checking stock, reserving, dispatching) as explicitly differentiated in the source text.

Structural Check
- [S1] STC11 failed: Each variable definition must have a valid range with at least two distinct values. | Variable `v1` has an invalid range `[]`. | Variable `v2` has an invalid range `[]`.
- [S2] STC16 failed: Every outgoing edge of XOR/OR branches must have exactly one guard. | XOR/OR edge `b1 -> n3` has 0 guards; exactly one is required. | XOR/OR edge `b1 -> n4` has 0 guards; exactly one is required. | XOR/OR edge `b2 -> n10` has 0 guards; exactly one is required. | XOR/OR edge `b2 -> n11` has 0 guards; exactly one is required.